course: dictionary
lesson: 13113
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word flipping is a good example. «She flipped the pancake high in the air» means turning it over quickly. «We flipped a coin to decide who went first» means tossing it so it lands on one side or the other.
explain: In Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, some people say flipping as a very mild swear word, to show annoyance or to add emphasis. «It's flipping freezing outside!» means it is very cold. Grown-ups sometimes say it, but it is not a word you should copy at school.
explain: The meaning can change again with a different word after it. «He flipped out when he lost the game» means he suddenly became very angry or upset. Flipped out is an informal phrase, so the words around it are the clue. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then try your meaning in it to check.
fact: Words with more than one meaning are called multiple-meaning words.
fact: «Flipping» can mean turning over quickly, as in «flipping pancakes».
fact: «Flipping» is also a mild swear word in the UK, Ireland and Australia, used to show annoyance, as in «It's flipping freezing».
fact: «Flipping out» is informal and means suddenly becoming very angry or upset.
fact: In maths, flipping a shape over makes a reflection, so the shape becomes a mirror image of itself.
exercise: «She flipped the pancake high in the air.» What does flipping mean in this sentence? | Shouting at someone | Falling asleep | Cooking it for a very long time | *Turning over quickly
exercise: «It's flipping freezing outside!» Which description fits flipping in this sentence? | A word for a cold drink | The name of a park | *A mild stand-in for a stronger swear word, to show annoyance | A number that means ten
exercise: «We flipped a coin to decide who went first.» Find and copy the word that shows what happened to the coin. | *flipped | first | coin | decide
test: «He flipped out when he lost the game.» What does flipped out mean? | Went outside to play | Won the game easily | *Suddenly became very angry or upset | Fell asleep on the sofa
test: Why might a grown-up say «flipping» instead of a stronger swear word? | Because it is the name of a country | *Because it is a softer, milder word to show annoyance | Because it is a number | Because it means hungry
exam: Which sentence uses flipping in the literal sense of turning over? | «Our teacher is flipping amazing.» | «It's flipping cold today.» | *«Dad flipped the burger on the grill.» | «Ben flipped out at the football match.»
